A||||1||billfredmike24||Amp power control wire to what wire on deck?||||1||
Z||000000||billfredmike24||09-16-2001||08:35 PM||||I have a pioneer deck and kenwood amp, what wire from the deck do i connect to the blue power control wire from the amp.  It works with the blue/white wire that comes from the deck that says remote control.  But in the pioneer manual it says "When an external power amp is being used, be sure not to connect the blue/white lead to the amp's power terminal.  Likewise do not connect the blue/white lead to the power terminal of the auto-antenna.  Such connection could cause excessive current drain and malfunction."<BR>So what wire do i connect it too.<BR>Also my deck has Sub.W light on it, it doesn't come on when the subs on, anyone know why.<BR>TIA Mike||||reg||1
Z||000001||gargoyle||09-16-2001||09:19 PM||||I think they are worried about somebody actually attaching the blue/white wire to the + power connection on the amp. It goes to the control connection. Actually what I usually do is connect that to a fused relay that has 12v coming directly from the battery. This way if you add multiple amps or other pieces that need to be controlled and you won't load down the head unit. I can't address the other question, I use Alpine.||||reg||1
